# L5c: L2 with 4K prefill chunks and CUDA graphs captured only up to 128 tokens per step.
# - 4K chunks: a step carrying a prefill chunk took about 1.41 s at 8K; at 4K, co-running sessions get twice the decode
#   steps through another session's cold prefill. L5p showed chunk size barely moves prefill speed. The smaller
#   activation peak and unprofiled FlashMLA buffer (256 KiB per batched token) also return memory to KV.
# - Capture cap 128: under the MTP schedule a decode step is at most 64 tokens for 16 sessions and 128 for 64, so
#   nothing in the measured range runs outside a graph. The default 512 costs about 4.5 GiB of graph memory per GPU
#   (inside the util budget) and doubles with max-model-len, which is what kept 1M context from fitting.
--served-model-name glm-5.3
--host 0.0.0.0
--port 8000
--trust-remote-code
--tensor-parallel-size 4
--enable-expert-parallel
--kv-cache-dtype fp8_ds_mla
--gpu-memory-utilization 0.92
--max-model-len 262144
--max-num-batched-tokens 4096
--max-cudagraph-capture-size 128
--speculative-config {"method":"mtp","num_speculative_tokens":5,"num_speculative_tokens_per_batch_size":[[1,4,5],[5,16,3],[17,1024,1]]}
--enable-prefix-caching
--enable-prompt-tokens-details
--enable-per-request-metrics
--enable-auto-tool-choice
--tool-call-parser glm47
--reasoning-parser glm45
--decode-context-parallel-size 4
--kv-offloading-size 300
--kv-offloading-backend native
--profiler-config {"profiler":"torch","torch_profiler_dir":"/root/results/profile","torch_profiler_with_stack":false}
